```
The polls below assume no open entry for this bug.

**3. AskUserQuestion — poll 1 of 2**

> **rdp-audio: pause?** Your "don't interrupt" sets aside the rule "compact a tab at 50–60% of its working memory used" (manifest §4). rdp-audio has used 70% (61k, 30% left). It is on task 7 of 9: the failing test is written, the implementation is in progress, and tasks 8–9 are not started. May I pause it between steps?
> - **Pause after task 7's commit, compact, resume (Recommended).** One queued message; it finishes and commits first. No `esc`, and no work is lost. It costs a few minutes.
> - **No pause, run to the end of task 9.** The rule is waived this once. It may auto-compact mid-task and lose parts of its brief.

**4. AskUserQuestion — poll 2 of 2**

> **noVNC fix: where?** Putting it into rdp-audio sets aside "one tab = one task" (§4: the fix would share that tab's assumptions, branch and PR) and "every new task is designed first" (§10a: two product advisors draft, two voting advisors approve, then an executor starts).
> - **Separate task: design starts now, own tab and branch (Recommended).** rdp-audio is untouched.
> - **Same tab, after task 9.** Both rules are waived this once; the fix ships in the RDP-audio PR.
> - **Own tab and branch, no design round.** The design rule is waived this once.

**5. On "pause"** (foreground; I send only if `"focused": false`):
```bash
herdr agent get rdp-audio
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "Finish the current step, commit, stop and report: phase, branch, head SHA, next step."
```
When the waiter fires, I read `<inbox>/rdp-audio.last`, run `herdr agent get rdp-audio`, and check the commit:
```bash
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio log -1 --format='%h %s'
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio status --short
```
Then, in the background:
```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "/compact mid-task: keep the brief, the decisions, DIR/branch/head SHA and the open items" --wait --timeout 300000; \
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-audio.last
```
After that, two background prompts in the same form:
- "One line: phase, branch, head SHA, next step."
- "Continue the plan with tasks 8-9 under the same brief: TDD, same worktree and branch. Reply in English."

